      "sourceHash": "ad7bac0fe0a0848fbfda88ea21e2db83ec8a715269b11a136b6ed607265abfa3",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 9,
          "en": "Now we saw how we can use grid column start end and grid row start and end to target different line numbers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 9,
          "end": 12.63,
          "en": "and are accurate to define where the elements should go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 12.63,
          "end": 17.74,
          "en": "Now working with the line numbers of course is an option but not the only one we got,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 17.76,
          "end": 26.76,
          "en": "it would also be nice to give our columns and rows names or to give our column and row lines names to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 26.76,
          "end": 30.87,
          "en": "be precise and we can do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 30.87,
          "end": 36.29,
          "en": "Let's start with the rows because we repeat the columns and there is something special about that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 36.3,
          "end": 37.21,
          "en": "I'll come back to that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 37.35,
          "end": 38.91,
          "en": "so let's start with the rows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 39.33,
          "end": 42.33,
          "en": "If we want to name line number one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 42.36,
          "end": 50.99,
          "en": "so this first horizontal line, then we have to add the name in front of the value for the first row, so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 51.06,
          "end": 52.69,
          "en": "of the height of the first row",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 53.01,
          "end": 55.81,
          "en": "and we add the name in square brackets, that's important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 55.81,
          "end": 56.9,
          "en": "this is required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 57.09,
          "end": 60.09,
          "en": "and then any name of your choice, you're totally free.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 60.09,
          "end": 62.97,
          "en": "You shouldn't take span though because it's a reserved word",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 62.97,
          "end": 65.49,
          "en": "but other than that, you're totally free.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 65.49,
          "end": 69,
          "en": "So for example here, we could name this row-1-start,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 69,
          "end": 71.33,
          "en": "however again, the name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 71.4,
          "end": 76.76,
          "en": "so row-1-start. After this first row,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 76.96000000000001,
          "end": 79.46000000000001,
          "en": "we name the line that comes thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 79.53,
          "end": 84.51,
          "en": "so line number two, the second horizontal line. We add square brackets again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 84.67,
          "end": 91.42,
          "en": "and now we can name this row-1-end. You could argue that it maybe also should be named row-2-start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 91.42,
          "end": 98.41,
          "en": "though because the second the line here actually is both the ending of the first row and the start of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 98.41,
          "end": 100.12,
          "en": "the second one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 100.12,
          "end": 101.5,
          "en": "Good thing is if you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 101.5,
          "end": 107.71000000000001,
          "en": "you can assign multiple names, simply by staying in the square brackets, adding a whitespace and adding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 107.8,
          "end": 110.64,
          "en": "the second name which of course is totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 110.82,
          "end": 111.85,
          "en": "This is not required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 111.85,
          "end": 112.99000000000001,
          "en": "you can do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 113.02000000000001,
          "end": 117.8,
          "en": "you can of course also use one name. This will refer to the same line, that's important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 117.91,
          "end": 121.3,
          "en": "so you can use the two names interchangeably now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 121.51,
          "end": 126.85,
          "en": "And now we can simply add another name after this additional row here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 126.91,
          "end": 133.47,
          "en": "so maybe we can name this row-2-end and we could also name it row-3-start if we wanted to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 133.48,
          "end": 140.5,
          "en": "so we could add row-3-start as a second name and then we can name the last line number which is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 140.53,
          "end": 141.02,
          "en": "row-3-end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 141.04,
          "end": 146.01,
          "en": "for example. If you save that and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 146.3,
          "end": 148.03,
          "en": "you don't see the names here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 148.07,
          "end": 154.22,
          "en": "in the inspector, that's not displayed. We can just check if it works because we can now reference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 154.22,
          "end": 156.37,
          "en": "these names instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 156.38,
          "end": 163.22,
          "en": "So in places where we refer to the row numbers, like here grid row start, we refer to line number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 163.22,
          "end": 164.07,
          "en": "two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 164.12,
          "end": 169.24,
          "en": "now a name for line number two is either row-1-end or row-2-start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 169.52,
          "end": 171.31,
          "en": "Let's maybe pick 2-start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 171.32,
          "end": 174.26,
          "en": "because here we are defining something which should start there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 174.5,
          "end": 179.53,
          "en": "so we set this to row-2-start, without square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 179.54,
          "end": 185.84,
          "en": "Now grid row end doesn't take a line number here because here we use the span syntax but for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 185.84,
          "end": 190.4,
          "en": "down there on element three, we get a grid row end of three,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 190.55,
          "end": 194.7,
          "en": "now line number three has that row-2-end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 194.7,
          "end": 198.45,
          "en": "name for example, we could also use row-3-start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 198.77,
          "end": 205.49,
          "en": "But let's take a row-2-end and let's replace grid row end, the value three to be precise with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 205.49,
          "end": 209.7,
          "en": "row-2-end, again without square brackets here and grid row",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 209.72,
          "end": 218.45,
          "en": "start of course could be row-1-start as a name, like that. With all that added, if we save everything and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 218.45,
          "end": 219.61,
          "en": "we reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 219.86,
          "end": 225.53,
          "en": "we shouldn't see any changes which is a good sign because that means it works because we target the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 225.53,
          "end": 231.41,
          "en": "same lines as before but this time, with our named lines here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
